'''''Trinchesia hamanni''''' is a [[species]] of [[sea slug]], an aeolid [[nudibranch]], a [[marine (ocean)|marine]] [[gastropod]] [[mollusc]] in the [[Family (taxonomy)|family]] [[Trinchesiidae]].<ref name="Korshunova">Korshunova T.; Fletcher K.; Martynov A. (2025). [https://doi.org/10.1093/zoolinnean/zlaf057 The endless forms are the most differentiated—how taxonomic pseudo-optimization masked natural diversity and evolution: the nudibranch case] Zoological Journal of the Linnean Society, Volume 204, Issue 4, August 2025, zlaf057, </ref>

==Distribution==
This species was described from [[La Jolla]], [[California]].<ref name=ssf>Rudman, W.B. (2005 October 4) [http://www.seaslugforum.net/factsheet/cuthhama ''Cuthona hamanni'' Behrens, 1987.] <nowiki>[In]</nowiki> Sea Slug Forum. Australian Museum, Sydney.</ref>

==Description==
The typical adult size of this species is 14&nbsp;mm.<ref name=ssf/>

